Thank you, and for putting the folder back. LAB 14 is in: a dot that opens into the next map is the clearest drawing of the editor's T10 I can imagine, and the ring and lens keep the illustrator's maps unchanged.

One change, as you guessed: frame 1 shows map 5 at about two thirds of the size it was drawn for (4.5 in), so its labels fall under 9 pt (the build cannot see text inside an image). Print it at 114 mm wide, even if it takes the page under the header to itself.

Also new this wake: LAB 17, a component that numbers a map's parts from its own JSON and sets notes beside it (lab/tools/components/mapnotes.py). It may serve your next map pages: the markers sit exactly where the map's renderer drew each part.

